### Variables
@authority = https://localhost:5001
@client1_id = client-1
@client1_secret = secret
@client1_redirect = https://localhost:5002/signin-oidc

### 1) Authorize request for client-1 (authorization code flow)
# .http files can't drive the login UI. Open this URL in a browser, sign in,
# then copy the `code` query parameter from the redirect to the next request below.
# https://localhost:5001/connect/authorize?client_id=client-1&redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A5002%2Fsignin-oidc&response_type=code&scope=openid%20profile%20api1&state=abc123
GET {{authority}}/connect/authorize?client_id={{client1_id}}&redirect_uri={{client1_redirect}}&response_type=code&scope=openid%20profile%20api1&state=abc123

### Paste the authorization code here
@auth_code = PASTE_AUTH_CODE_HERE

### 2) Exchange the code for a token (client-1)
POST {{authority}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code&client_id={{client1_id}}&client_secret={{client1_secret}}&code={{auth_code}}&redirect_uri={{client1_redirect}}

> {%
    client.global.set("subject_token", response.body.access_token);
%}

### 3) Token exchange: swap client-1's access token for a token scoped to api2
POST {{authority}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange&client_id={{client1_id}}&client_secret={{client1_secret}}&subject_token={{subject_token}}&subject_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:access_token&requested_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:access_token&scope=api2

> {%
    client.global.set("exchanged_token", response.body.access_token);
%}

### Variables for the requesting client (client-2, e.g. an API doing on-behalf-of)
@client2_id = client-2
@client2_secret = secret

### 4) ISSUE REPRO: client-2 exchanges client-1's token
# RFC 8693 §1 / §4.3: the client making the exchange request (client-2) is the
# client, so `client_id` in the issued token should be "client-2".
POST {{authority}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange&client_id={{client2_id}}&client_secret={{client2_secret}}&subject_token={{subject_token}}&subject_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:access_token&requested_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:access_token&scope=api2

> {%
    client.global.set("exchanged_token_client2", response.body.access_token);
%}

### Variables for the second requesting client (client-3)
@client3_id = client-3
@client3_secret = secret

### 5) ISSUE REPRO: nested `act`
# Run step 4 first. Its token (scope api2) has aud=client-3, so client-3 may exchange it
POST {{authority}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange&client_id={{client3_id}}&client_secret={{client3_secret}}&subject_token={{exchanged_token_client2}}&subject_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:access_token&requested_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:access_token&scope=api2
